# ==============================================================================
# CURSOR & AI CODING RULES FOR lib-ifactory-os-v2
# ==============================================================================
# This file governs all AI-assisted coding and automated edits in this repository.
# Adhere strictly to these rules to prevent merge conflicts, architecture breakage,
# and unnecessary file modifications.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. ARCHITECTURAL INVARIANTS & SCOPE BOUNDARIES
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# - This repository is a monorepo containing:
#     1) Core OS Shell: `src/lib/os/`, `src/lib/appShell/`
#     2) Product Flavors: `src/lib/os/flavors/` (`cloud`, `ioware`)
#     3) Modular Apps: `src/pms-app/`, `src/aps-app/`, `src/ocr-app/`, etc.
#
# - STRICT LAYER SEPARATION:
#   * Apps must NEVER leak into OS core files or flavor files.
#   * NEVER import an app store (e.g., `pmsStore`, `hmi-store`) into `src/lib/os/` or `src/lib/os/flavors/`.
#   * OS must remain 100% agnostic of specific app internal state.
#
# - BLAST RADIUS ENFORCEMENT:
#   * When working on an app (e.g., `src/pms-app/`), edit ONLY files within that app's directory.
#   * NEVER touch unrelated apps (e.g., `src/ocr-app/`, `src/aps-app/`) or root configuration files.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. STRICT "DO NOT TOUCH" ZONE (PROTECTED FILES)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEVER modify the following files unless explicitly requested by the user:
#   - Build & Config:
#       * `svelte.config.js`
#       * `vite.config.ts`
#       * `tsconfig.json`
#       * `package.json` / `package-lock.json`
#       * `.lintstagedrc.json` / `commitlint.config.js`
#   - Core OS Shell Architecture:
#       * `src/lib/appShell/AppShell.svelte`
#       * `src/lib/os/Desktop.svelte`
#       * `src/lib/os/IFactoryOS.svelte`
#       * `src/lib/os/TaskBar.svelte`
#       * `src/lib/os/index.svelte.ts`
#       * `src/lib/os/flavors/types.ts`
#   - Deployment & Tooling:
#       * `release.sh`
#       * `Dockerfile*`
#       * `resources/*`
#       * `ota-templates/*`

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. AUTHENTICATION & SHELL CHROME INTEGRITY
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# - AUTHENTICATION BELONGS TO THE OS LOCKSCREEN:
#   * Operator/User login, credentials verification, and session lifecycle are handled
#     exclusively by `src/lib/os/Lockscreen.ioware.svelte` (for ioWare) or `Lockscreen.svelte` (cloud).
#   * NEVER create an in-app login page (e.g., `MachineLogin.svelte`).
#   * NEVER gate app routes behind an in-app login check when the OS lockscreen exists.
#   * Edge HMI apps (like `pms-app`) must assume the operator is already authenticated
#     once the app opens, starting directly at the operational entry point (e.g., `StartJob`).
#
# - SHELL CHROME IS IMMUTABLE:
#   * Do NOT add visibility toggles or hooks to hide the OS MenuBar or TaskBar
#     (e.g., `showTopbar`, `isTopbarVisible`, `taskBar.visible`).
#   * MenuBar and TaskBar must always remain visible and managed by `IFactoryOS.svelte`.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. COMPONENT REUSE & DESIGN SYSTEM FIRST
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# - BEFORE writing any new component or raw HTML, ALWAYS check:
#     1) `@ifactory/ui-v2`: `Button`, `Input`, `Label`, `Dialog`, `Keyboard`, `Tabs`, etc.
#     2) Shared OS primitives: `src/lib/components/`
#     3) Existing App components: e.g. `TimerDisplay.svelte`, `Stat.svelte`,
#        `StatusBanner.svelte`, `ReasonSummaryCard.svelte`, `SectionHeading.svelte`, `JobHeader.svelte`.
#
# - NEVER reinvent existing wheels:
#   * Timers, countdowns, metric badges, confirmation dialogs, and headers already exist.
#   * Reuse existing styles and tokens:
#       - Primary Brand: `#FF6C2E` (Accent Orange)
#       - Dark Base: `#222222` / `#1B2028`
#       - Error / Alert: `#EF4444` / `status-error`
#       - Success / Online: `status-online`
#       - Typography: `Space Grotesk` (headings/metrics), `Manrope` (body/details)

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. SAFE "WIPE CODING" & NON-DESTRUCTIVE EDITS
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# - When rewriting or refactoring a screen:
#   * PRESERVE all existing business logic:
#       - Timers & intervals (`setInterval`, live duration counters).
#       - Active subscriptions (MQTT handlers, store bindings).
#       - Navigation transitions & prefilled state parameters.
#   * NEVER silently drop existing functional features (e.g., live stopped timers).
#   * Do NOT introduce formatting diffs or `<!-- svelte-ignore -->` comments into untouched files.
#   * Keep diffs surgical, focused, and review-friendly.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6. VERIFICATION & PRE-COMMIT QUALITY GATES
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# - Before considering any task complete:
#     1) Run `git status` and `git diff --stat`: Verify that ONLY expected files are modified.
#     2) Run `npm run check` (svelte-check): Verify zero TypeScript or Svelte compilation errors.
#     3) Run `npm run lint`: Verify ESLint and Prettier formatting compliance.
